{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781307436541,"sessionID":"ses_141cdb3a1ffeB9z406SOb13Vxo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_bdrk_01EZJVCZzu8LVEgG6L3BCAAL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/batch_transcription_queue_20260509/spec.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/batch_transcription_queue_20260509/spec.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Track: Batch Transcription Queue\n2: \n3: ## Problem\n4: Users must transcribe media files one at a time. There is no way to queue multiple files for overnight or background processing.\n5: \n6: ## Goal\n7: Add a batch queue where users can drop multiple media files and have them transcribed sequentially with progress tracking.\n8: \n9: ## Acceptance Criteria\n10: - [ ] Batch queue accepts multiple media files via file picker or drag-and-drop\n11: - [ ] Queue persists to SQLite (survives app restart)\n12: - [ ] Sequential processing with per-file progress\n13: - [ ] Results saved to library automatically on completion\n14: - [ ] Cancel/pause individual items or entire queue\n15: - [ ] Tests pass\n16: - [ ] Build and vet clean\n\n(End of file - total 16 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Track: Batch Transcription Queue\n\n## Problem\nUsers must transcribe media files one at a time. There is no way to queue multiple files for overnight or background processing.\n\n## Goal\nAdd a batch queue where users can drop multiple media files and have them transcribed sequentially with progress tracking.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Batch queue accepts multiple media files via file picker or drag-and-drop\n- [ ] Queue persists to SQLite (survives app restart)\n- [ ] Sequential processing with per-file progress\n- [ ] Results saved to library automatically on completion\n- [ ] Cancel/pause individual items or entire queue\n- [ ] Tests pass\n- [ ] Build and vet clean","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/tracks/batch_transcription_queue_20260509/spec.md","text":"# Track: Batch Transcription Queue\n\n## Problem\nUsers must transcribe media files one at a time. There is no way to queue multiple files for overnight or background processing.\n\n## Goal\nAdd a batch queue where users can drop multiple media files and have them transcribed sequentially with progress tracking.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Batch queue accepts multiple media files via file picker or drag-and-drop\n- [ ] Queue persists to SQLite (survives app restart)\n- [ ] Sequential processing with per-file progress\n- [ ] Results saved to library automatically on completion\n- [ ] Cancel/pause individual items or entire queue\n- [ ] Tests pass\n- [ ] Build and vet clean","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":16,"totalLines":16,"truncated":false}},"title":"measure/tracks/batch_transcription_queue_20260509/spec.md","time":{"start":1781307436375,"end":1781307436525}},"id":"prt_ebe326cc8001X3zm40w5rLHj4M","sessionID":"ses_141cdb3a1ffeB9z406SOb13Vxo","messageID":"msg_ebe324e1600164C4E4IIY9yFMV"}}
