{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781307486303,"sessionID":"ses_141cdb3a1ffeB9z406SOb13Vxo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_bdrk_01K9fCsynWMYdcYnVXtQALFs","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/lessons-learned.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/lessons-learned.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Lessons Learned\n2: \n3: > Greenfield reset. Entries below are timeless principles carried into the rewrite. Remove or replace as the new implementation matures.\n4: \n5: ## Go + GTK4 + GStreamer\n6: \n7: - **Thread Safety:** Always route GTK UI updates through `glib.IdleAdd`. Direct widget access from goroutines causes crashes.\n8: - **Headless Tests:** Skip tests requiring a display or hardware with `t.Skip`. Mock GStreamer pipelines and cloud providers in unit tests.\n9: - **GTK Initialization Detection:** `DISPLAY`/`WAYLAND_DISPLAY` env vars alone do not guarantee a usable GTK display. Tests that create GTK widgets must attempt `gtk.Init()` and skip on panic to remain CI-stable.\n10: - **GStreamer Path Safety:** Sanitize every file path before interpolating it into a pipeline description. Prefer element properties over string interpolation where possible.\n11: - **Binary Search for Timestamps:** Use O(log n) lookup for word-by-time queries, not linear scans.\n12: - **Context Cancellation:** Pass `context.Context` through async operations (transcription, export, recording) so they stop cleanly on app shutdown.\n13: - **Provider Abstraction:** Keep OpenAI/Google/local transcription details behind a single interface in `internal/ai`. No SDK imports in UI or app controller.\n14: - **Database Migrations:** Use a versioned `schema_migrations` table from day one. Avoid ad-hoc column-backfill helpers.\n15: - **SQLite Concurrency:** Set `PRAGMA busy_timeout` and `PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL` on every SQLite connection to avoid `SQLITE_BUSY` when background goroutines and tests access the database concurrently.\n16: \n17: ## General\n18: \n19: - **MVP First:** Build the smallest end-to-end flow (record/import → transcribe → playback → delete word → export) before adding advanced features.\n20: - **Tests Before UI:** Verify media pipeline correctness with real fixtures before wiring it to GTK widgets.\n21: - **Keep main.go Small:** The application controller belongs in `internal/app`, not the entry point.\n\n(End of file - total 21 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Lessons Learned\n\n> Greenfield reset. Entries below are timeless principles carried into the rewrite. Remove or replace as the new implementation matures.\n\n## Go + GTK4 + GStreamer\n\n- **Thread Safety:** Always route GTK UI updates through `glib.IdleAdd`. Direct widget access from goroutines causes crashes.\n- **Headless Tests:** Skip tests requiring a display or hardware with `t.Skip`. Mock GStreamer pipelines and cloud providers in unit tests.\n- **GTK Initialization Detection:** `DISPLAY`/`WAYLAND_DISPLAY` env vars alone do not guarantee a usable GTK display. Tests that create GTK widgets must attempt `gtk.Init()` and skip on panic to remain CI-stable.\n- **GStreamer Path Safety:** Sanitize every file path before interpolating it into a pipeline description. Prefer element properties over string interpolation where possible.\n- **Binary Search for Timestamps:** Use O(log n) lookup for word-by-time queries, not linear scans.\n- **Context Cancellation:** Pass `context.Context` through async operations (transcription, export, recording) so they stop cleanly on app shutdown.\n- **Provider Abstraction:** Keep OpenAI/Google/local transcription details behind a single interface in `internal/ai`. No SDK imports in UI or app controller.\n- **Database Migrations:** Use a versioned `schema_migrations` table from day one. Avoid ad-hoc column-backfill helpers.\n- **SQLite Concurrency:** Set `PRAGMA busy_timeout` and `PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL` on every SQLite connection to avoid `SQLITE_BUSY` when background goroutines and tests access the database concurrently.\n\n## General\n\n- **MVP First:** Build the smallest end-to-end flow (record/import → transcribe → playback → delete word → export) before adding advanced features.\n- **Tests Before UI:** Verify media pipeline correctness with real fixtures before wiring it to GTK widgets.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/verbal/measure/lessons-learned.md","text":"# Lessons Learned\n\n> Greenfield reset. Entries below are timeless principles carried into the rewrite. Remove or replace as the new implementation matures.\n\n## Go + GTK4 + GStreamer\n\n- **Thread Safety:** Always route GTK UI updates through `glib.IdleAdd`. Direct widget access from goroutines causes crashes.\n- **Headless Tests:** Skip tests requiring a display or hardware with `t.Skip`. Mock GStreamer pipelines and cloud providers in unit tests.\n- **GTK Initialization Detection:** `DISPLAY`/`WAYLAND_DISPLAY` env vars alone do not guarantee a usable GTK display. Tests that create GTK widgets must attempt `gtk.Init()` and skip on panic to remain CI-stable.\n- **GStreamer Path Safety:** Sanitize every file path before interpolating it into a pipeline description. Prefer element properties over string interpolation where possible.\n- **Binary Search for Timestamps:** Use O(log n) lookup for word-by-time queries, not linear scans.\n- **Context Cancellation:** Pass `context.Context` through async operations (transcription, export, recording) so they stop cleanly on app shutdown.\n- **Provider Abstraction:** Keep OpenAI/Google/local transcription details behind a single interface in `internal/ai`. No SDK imports in UI or app controller.\n- **Database Migrations:** Use a versioned `schema_migrations` table from day one. Avoid ad-hoc column-backfill helpers.\n- **SQLite Concurrency:** Set `PRAGMA busy_timeout` and `PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL` on every SQLite connection to avoid `SQLITE_BUSY` when background goroutines and tests access the database concurrently.\n\n## General\n\n- **MVP First:** Build the smallest end-to-end flow (record/import → transcribe → playback → delete word → export) before adding advanced features.\n- **Tests Before UI:** Verify media pipeline correctness with real fixtures before wiring it to GTK widgets.\n- **Keep main.go Small:** The application controller belongs in `internal/app`, not the entry point.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":21,"totalLines":21,"truncated":false}},"title":"measure/lessons-learned.md","time":{"start":1781307485944,"end":1781307486287}},"id":"prt_ebe332b18001MrRSJ1OVtleEEG","sessionID":"ses_141cdb3a1ffeB9z406SOb13Vxo","messageID":"msg_ebe3314e00018P17jXe0cF1xY1"}}
